meta {
  name: Customer Onboarding API
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: authorization_code
  callback_url: bruno://auth
  authorization_url: {{idp_base_url}}/connect/authorize
  access_token_url: {{idp_base_url}}/connect/token
  refresh_token_url: {{idp_base_url}}/connect/token
  client_id: {{idp_client_id}}
  client_secret:
  scope: {{idp_scope}}
  state:
  pkce: true
  credentials_placement: body
  credentials_id: customer_onboarding
  token_placement: header
  token_header_prefix: Bearer
  auto_fetch_token: true
  auto_refresh_token: true
}

docs {
  # Customer Onboarding API

  V3 Customer Onboarding bounded-context API.

  ## Authentication

  The collection uses native Bruno OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code + PKCE.

  Bruno opens the Duende IdentityServer authorization endpoint, obtains an
  authorization code, performs the PKCE token exchange, and attaches the
  resulting access token as a Bearer token.

  No API endpoint in this collection bypasses `[Authorize]`.

  ## Local endpoints

  API:
  `https://customer-api.dev.localhost:44363`

  IdentityServer:
  `https://idp.dev.localhost:44392`

  ## Test persona

  The intended initial test persona is the Customer Service Agent:

  `sophie.cs`

  The password is deliberately not stored in this collection. Bruno's native
  OAuth browser flow presents the IdentityServer login page and the tester
  enters the credential there.

  ## OAuth client

  `idp_client_id` and `idp_scope` are environment values because the exact
  client registration remains owned by the Duende IdentityServer configuration.
}
